s"] "\n" [:option {:value "1615"} "1924"] "\n" [:option {:value "905000"} "1928"] "\n" [:option {:value "905175"} "1936"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/364"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Military Ski Patrol, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} " 8 February 1948"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic (non-medal)"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/153"} "Skistadion, St. Moritz"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/905176"} "32 from 8 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "27 km."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "At the 1948 Winter Olympics, in St. Moritz, Switzerland, the last military patrol competition was held as a demonstration sport. This was in part to the aftermath of World War II, which decimated Europe. This sport would be superseded by the " [:a {:href "/results/1515"} "biathlon competition"] " which debuted at the " [:a {:href "/editions/36"} "1960 Winter Olympics"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The cross-country ski run was not prepared, and was made by the leading Swiss team. The Czechoslovak participant " [:a {:href "/athletes/900708"} "Karel Dvořák"] " described the weather of the day as extremely mild, with temperatures of about 0° C at the starting point at the upper cableway station (2,486 m), on top of the Corviglia, in the morning. The participants wore military equipment, 10 kg of baggage on the back and a military rifle. Only the officers, the patrol leaders, had pistols, and did not compete in shooting. At the shooting range, they had to shoot on three rubber balloons at a distance of 150 m. Every hit gave a bonus of one minute for the team."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Switzerland won fairly easily, by three minutes over Finland. Switzerland had by far the best ski time, about seven minutes ahead of the Finns, and six minutes ahead of Sweden, but Finland received nine shooting bonus minutes, while the Swiss had only five. Sweden also outskied the Finns, but the Finnish dominance with the rifle moved the Swedes back to third place."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {} "Shooting Time Bonus"] [:th {} "Ski Time"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "Switzerland"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SUI"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SUI.png"}] "SUI"]] [:td {} "2-34:25"] [:td {} "5:00"] [:td {} "2-39:25"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "11"} [:a {:href "/athletes/99284"} "Robert Zurbriggen"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/900589"} "Arnold Andenmatten"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/900643"} "Vital Vouardoux"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/900650"} "Heinrich Zurbriggen"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} "Finland"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FIN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FIN.png"}] "FIN"]] [:td {} "2-37:23"] [:td {} "9:00"] [:td {} "2-46:23"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "11"} [:a {:href "/athletes/900199"} "Eero Naapuri"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/42059"} "Vilho Ylönen"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/900198"} "Mikko Meriläinen"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/900189"} "Tauno Honkanen"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} "Sweden"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SWE"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SWE.png"}] "SWE"]] [:td {} "2-41:03"] [:td {} "4:00"] [:td {} "2-45:03"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :